    "media:imagetext": "PAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS PHOTO\nFIRST LONG RANGE CLIPPER\nBuilt according to Pan American World Airways' specifications in\n1934, the Sikorsky 42 was the first truly long range airliner. Powered by\nfour engines, the S-42 carried 32 passengers at a cruising speed of 145 miles\nper hour. The S-42 broke nine world's records in its test flights and com-\npleted a round-trip, nonstop flight of 2,500 miles between Miami and the\nVirgin Islands. The S-42 was also used on the original survey flights over\nboth the Atlantic and Pacific routes.\n#\n#\nPAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS\n135 East 42nd Street\nNew York 17, New York\nOXford 7-6300",
